+## 6. Notes for the implementation section of the paper (v5, in English)
+
+* **Offloaded stages.** Per picture: (i) gradients, 4x4 classification and transpose index; (ii) encoder Wiener statistics (luma/chroma covariance per ASU and class); (iii) the parallel part of the filter derivation: greedy merging of the 25 classes (one 13x13 Cholesky solve per candidate pair, 300 pairs in the first step) and the Wiener solve, quantisation and coefficient refinement of all 325 (number-of-filters, filter) hypotheses; (iv) luma filtering with the geometric transform; (v) CCALF statistics. The CPU keeps the sequential decisions (CABAC rate estimation, CTU on/off, filter-set selection, APS), chroma filtering and CCALF filtering.
+* **Bit-exactness.** Integer stages are exact by construction. Float stages reproduce the CPU order of operations: integer per-block sums, then one thread per accumulated element walking the blocks in CPU order (IEEE `__fadd_rn`); the derivation kernels are compiled without FMA contraction (`--fmad=false`) and use IEEE division/sqrt; ties in the merge step are resolved as in the CPU loop (smallest cost, then first pair). A verification mode compares every sample, class, covariance value, merge level, coefficient, clipping index and error value bit by bit; bitstreams are identical to the original VVenC.
+* **Fixed-cost reduction.** The original picture is uploaded asynchronously when the picture starts (overlapped with CTU encoding); classification and statistics are one submission with a single synchronisation; the pre-ALF picture buffer is page-locked once (direct 2D DMA, no staging copy); classes are not downloaded unless the CPU needs them; the picture stays resident on the GPU from the statistics to the CCALF statistics; small pictures use a single pipeline chunk.
+* **Measurement.** `std::chrono::steady_clock` scopes around every ALF/CCALF task and around each sub-stage of the derivation (parallel vs. sequential part), CUDA events for H2D / kernels / D2H, RAPL (Linux powercap) for the CPU package energy inside the ALF scopes, NVML energy counter and 2 ms power sampling for the GPU, gated to the time in which the ALF is active, idle baselines subtracted.
